backported>\n\n'}, {'role': 'system', 'content': "1. a patch based on a newer version: \nFrom 743eb6c68d3534e01e73d316ddcaa7334c0e29d3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001\nFrom: Pierre-Louis Bossart <pierre-louis.bossart@linux.intel.com>\nDate: Tue, 13 Feb 2024 12:12:41 +0200\nSubject: [PATCH] ASoC: SOF: topology: dynamically allocate and store DAI\n widget->private\nMIME-Version: 1.0\nContent-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8\nContent-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit\n\nFor dspless mode, we need to allocate and store an 'sdai'\nstructure. The existing code allocate the data on the stack and does\nnot set the widget->private pointer.\n\nThis minor change should not have any impact on existing DAIs, even\nwhen the DSP is used.\n\nSigned-off-by: Pierre-Louis Bossart <pierre-louis.bossart@linux.intel.com>\nReviewed-by: Péter Ujfalusi <peter.ujfalusi@linux.intel.com>\nReviewed-by: Bard Liao <yung-chuan.liao@linux.intel.com>\nSigned-off-by: Peter Ujfalusi <peter.ujfalusi@linux.intel.com>\nLink: https://msgid.link/r/20240213101247.28887-10-peter.ujfalusi@linux.intel.com\nSigned-off-by: Mark Brown <broonie@kernel.org>\n\ndiff --git a/sound/soc/sof/topology.c b/sound/soc/sof/topology.c\nindex 25fb0d1443b6..915c2e88e32b 100644\n--- a/sound/soc/sof/topology.c\n+++ b/sound/soc/sof/topology.c\n@@ -2356,23 +2356,29 @@ static int sof_dspless_widget_ready(struct snd_soc_component *scomp, int index,\n \tif (WIDGET_IS_DAI(w->id)) {\n \t\tstruct snd_sof_dev *sdev = snd_soc_component_get_drvdata(scomp);\n \t\tstruct snd_sof_widget *swidget;\n-\t\tstruct snd_sof_dai dai;\n+\t\tstruct snd_sof_dai *sdai;\n \t\tint ret;\n \n \t\tswidget = kzalloc(sizeof(*swidget), GFP_KERNEL);\n \t\tif (!swidget)\n \t\t\treturn -ENOMEM;\n \n-\t\tmemset(&dai, 0, sizeof(dai));\n+\t\tsdai = kzalloc(sizeof(*sdai), GFP_KERNEL);\n+\t\tif (!sdai) {\n+\t\t\tkfree(swidget);\n+\t\t\treturn -ENOMEM;\n+\t\t}\n \n-\t\tret = sof_connect_dai_widget(scomp, w, tw, &dai);\n+\t\tret = sof_connect_dai_widget(scomp, w, tw, sdai);\n \t\tif (ret) {\n \t\t\tkfree(swidget);\n+\t\t\tkfree(sdai);\n \t\t\treturn ret;\n \t\t}\n \n \t\tswidget->scomp = scomp;\n \t\tswidget->widget = w;\n+\t\tswidget->private = sdai;\n \t\tmutex_init(&swidget->setup_mutex);\n \t\tw->dobj.private = swidget;\n \t\tlist_add(&swidget->list, &sdev->widget_list);\n"}, {'role': 'system', 'content': "2. the diff info between the newer version and and older version: \nFrom 743eb6c68d3534e01e73d316ddcaa7334c0e29d3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001\nFrom: Pierre-Louis Bossart <pierre-louis.bossart@linux.intel.com>\nDate: Tue, 13 Feb 2024 12:12:41 +0200\nSubject: [PATCH] ASoC: SOF: topology: dynamically allocate and store DAI\n widget->private\nMIME-Version: 1.0\nContent-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8\nContent-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit\n\nFor dspless mode, we need to allocate and store an 'sdai'\nstructure. The existing code allocate the data on the stack and does\nnot set the widget->private pointer.\n\nThis minor change should not have any impact on existing DAIs, even\nwhen the DSP is used.\n\nSigned-off-by: Pierre-Louis Bossart <pierre-louis.bossart@linux.intel.com>\nReviewed-by: Péter Ujfalusi <peter.ujfalusi@linux.intel.com>\nReviewed-by: Bard Liao <yung-chuan.liao@linux.intel.com>\nSigned-off-by: Peter Ujfalusi <peter.ujfalusi@linux.intel.com>\nLink: https://msgid.link/r/20240213101247.28887-10-peter.ujfalusi@linux.intel.com\nSigned-off-by: Mark Brown <broonie@kernel.org>\n\ndiff --git a/sound/soc/sof/topology.c b/sound/soc/sof/topology.c\nindex 25fb0d1443b6..915c2e88e32b 100644\n--- a/sound/soc/sof/topology.c\n+++ b/sound/soc/sof/topology.c\n@@ -2356,23 +2356,29 @@ static int sof_dspless_widget_ready(struct snd_soc_component *scomp, int index,\n \tif (WIDGET_IS_DAI(w->id)) {\n \t\tstruct snd_sof_dev *sdev = snd_soc_component_get_drvdata(scomp);\n \t\tstruct snd_sof_widget *swidget;\n-\t\tstruct snd_sof_dai dai;\n+\t\tstruct snd_sof_dai *sdai;\n \t\tint ret;\n \n \t\tswidget = kzalloc(sizeof(*swidget), GFP_KERNEL);\n \t\tif (!swidget)\n \t\t\treturn -ENOMEM;\n \n-\t\tmemset(&dai, 0, sizeof(dai));\n+\t\tsdai = kzalloc(sizeof(*sdai), GFP_KERNEL);\n+\t\tif (!sdai) {\n+\t\t\tkfree(swidget);\n+\t\t\treturn -ENOMEM;\n+\t\t}\n \n-\t\tret = sof_connect_dai_widget(scomp, w, tw, &dai);\n+\t\tret = sof_connect_dai_widget(scomp, w, tw, sdai);\n \t\tif (ret) {\n \t\t\tkfree(swidget);\n+\t\t\tkfree(sdai);\n \t\t\treturn ret;\n \t\t}\n \n \t\tswidget->scomp = scomp;\n \t\tswidget->widget = w;\n+\t\tswidget->private = sdai;\n \t\tmutex_init(&swidget->setup_mutex);\n \t\tw->dobj.private = swidget;\n \t\tlist_add(&swidget->list, &sdev->widget_list);\n\n===end==="}, {'role': 'user', 'content': 'Please return the final result.'}], 'response': 'A. Commit message:\nASoC: SOF: topology: dynamically allocate and store DAI widget->private\n\nB. Change summary:\nThe patch modifies the function `sof_dspless_widget_ready` to dynamically allocate a `snd_sof_dai` structure (`sdai`) instead of using a stack-allocated variable. This change ensures that the `widget->private` pointer is properly set, which is necessary for the dspless mode. Additionally, error handling has been updated to free allocated memory in case of failure.\n\nC. Compatibility Risk:\nLow\n\nD. Fixed Code:\ndiff --git a/sound/soc/sof/topology.c b/sound/soc/sof/topology.c\nindex 25fb0d1443b6..915c2e88e32b 100644\n--- a/sound/soc/sof/topology.c\n+++ b/sound/soc/sof/topology.c\n@@ -2356,23 +2356,29 @@ static int sof_dspless_widget_ready(struct snd_soc_component *scomp, int index,\n \tif (WIDGET_IS_DAI(w->id)) {\n \t\tstruct snd_sof_dev *sdev = snd_soc_component_get_drvdata(scomp);\n \t\tstruct snd_sof_widget *swidget;\n-\t\tstruct snd_sof_dai dai;\n+\t\tstruct snd_sof_dai *sdai;\n \t\tint ret;\n \n \t\tswidget = kzalloc(sizeof(*swidget), GFP_KERNEL);\n \t\tif (!swidget)\n \t\t\treturn -ENOMEM;\n \n-\t\tmemset(&dai, 0, sizeof(dai));\n+\t\tsdai = kzalloc(sizeof(*sdai), GFP_KERNEL);\n+\t\tif (!sdai) {\n+\t\t\tkfree(swidget);\n+\t\t\treturn -ENOMEM;\n+\t\t}\n \n-\t\tret = sof_connect_dai_widget(scomp, w, tw, &dai);\n+\t\tret = sof_connect_dai_widget(scomp, w, tw, sdai);\n \t\tif (ret) {\n \t\t\tkfree(swidget);\n+\t\t\tkfree(sdai);\n \t\t\treturn ret;\n \t\t}\n \n \t\tswidget->scomp = scomp;\n \t\tswidget->widget = w;\n+\t\tswidget->private = sdai;\n \t\tmutex_init(&swidget->setup_mutex);\n \t\tw->dobj.private = swidget;\n \t\tlist_add(&swidget->list, &sdev->widget_list);', 'request_token': 0, 'response_token': 0}]
